{:edb/db-before-t 678 :edb/db-after-t 679 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533991 50 #inst "2026-10-06T00:03:21.039Z" 13194139533991 true] [17592186087785 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275791 13194139533991 true] [17592186087785 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275815 13194139533991 true] [17592186087786 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275798 13194139533991 true] [17592186087786 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275805 13194139533991 true] [17592186087786 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275808 13194139533991 true] [17592186275791 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275792 13194139533991 true] [17592186275791 1089 "q-159757" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275791 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533991 true] [17592186275791 1100 "If $z=-9-\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275791 1113 #uuid "1fd36fc1-63ec-5bb6-9f2e-ae3a7bacac73" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275791 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-9-\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=-9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(-9) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-9-\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-9+\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(-9-\\text{i})+(-9+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-9+(-9))+\\text{i}(-1+1) \\\\  & =-18+\\text{i}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275793 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275794 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275795 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275796 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275797 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1041 "selection" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275795 13194139533991 true] [17592186275792 1110 #uuid "be9f873f-41b2-5d03-bf29-080478d28cb0" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275793 1034 "-8" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275793 1111 #uuid "26ead20b-1638-5e20-b8ae-c63ed579dd32" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275794 1034 "-10" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275794 1111 #uuid "4a0d23eb-f670-5df0-be8c-a2e3beac9197" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275795 1034 "-18" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275795 1111 #uuid "0fca5931-9374-5543-a9ff-2701cee97ed5" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275796 1034 "-18\\text{i}" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275796 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275796 1111 #uuid "aa9e47d5-bfd0-5712-93b2-413a7c93a998" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275797 1034 "-8\\text{i}" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275797 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275797 1111 #uuid "40aebf18-4cef-50e6-8ed1-e0d0dbb1242b" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275798 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275799 13194139533991 true] [17592186275798 1089 "q-16423" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275798 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533991 true] [17592186275798 1100 "Given that $z=4+9\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275798 1113 #uuid "36be1609-5bc0-56c1-a611-ac1989b2ace1" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275798 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=4,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=4-9\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(4+9\\text{i})(4-9\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+(4)(-9)\\text{i}+(4)(9)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(9)^{2} \\\\  & =16-36\\text{i}+36\\text{i}-(-1)(81) \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275800 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275801 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275802 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275803 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275804 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1041 "selection" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275803 13194139533991 true] [17592186275799 1110 #uuid "6a75804f-d387-5b0f-abe7-fbe0278a0d9b" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275800 1034 "97\\text{i}" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275800 1111 #uuid "791c85f6-036e-5302-b391-62dada87e528" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275801 1034 "85" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275801 1111 #uuid "03a6240a-d4f7-531b-845f-02448db67f2a" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275802 1034 "65" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275802 1111 #uuid "4684b083-df53-50af-ba80-13a6e06b94f3" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275803 1034 "97" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275803 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275803 1111 #uuid "b2579262-e10b-5a90-b3ee-f53be20c0c58" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275804 1034 "85\\text{i}" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275804 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275804 1111 #uuid "df9e7888-d2be-5bd0-8330-508007d20767" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275805 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275806 13194139533991 true] [17592186275805 1089 "q-279477" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275805 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533991 true] [17592186275805 1100 "If $z=-2-11\\text{i}$, then $z\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." 13194139533991 true] [17592186275805 1113 #uuid "594c5e35-b6c4-57d7-b7e2-3344f7754685" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275805 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-2-11\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-2,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-11,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+(-11)^{2} \\\\  & =4+121 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-2-11\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-2+11\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-2-11\\text{i})(-2+11\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(2)^{2}+(-2)(11)\\text{i}+(-11)(-2)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(11)^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\cancel{22\\text{i}}+\\cancel{22\\text{i}}-(-1)(121) \\\\  & =25+100 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275806 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275807 13194139533991 true] [17592186275806 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533991 true] [17592186275806 1041 "field-1" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275806 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275807 13194139533991 true] [17592186275806 1110 #uuid "b307d44c-8fdb-53b6-81af-2885341cf98b" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275807 1034 "125" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275807 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533991 true] [17592186275807 1111 #uuid "1413da37-d531-576a-9d27-31157308f6eb" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275808 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275809 13194139533991 true] [17592186275808 1089 "q-72284" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275808 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533991 true] [17592186275808 1100 "Given that $z=-1-7\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275808 1113 #uuid "786b081b-3937-58d9-97f1-dc3dd953af4b" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275808 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-1,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-7,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-7)^{2} \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-1+7\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-1-7\\text{i})(-1+7\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-1)(7)\\text{i}+(-7)(-1)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(7)^{2} \\\\  & =1-7\\text{i}+7\\text{i}-(-1)(49) \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533991 true] [17592186275809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275810 13194139533991 true] [17592186275809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275811 13194139533991 true] [17592186275809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275812 13194139533991 true] [17592186275809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275813 13194139533991 true] [17592186275809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275814 13194139533991 true] 